== MP changes ==
Based on preliminary results, there were 40 new MPs: 22 for Labour, 5 for National, 9 for ACT, 3 for the Greens, and 1 for the Māori Party.<ref>{{Cite news |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |title=Election 2020: The 40 diverse new MPs entering Parliament |url= https://www.newstalkzb.co.nz/news/vote-2020/election-2020-the-forty-newcomers-entering-parliament/ |access-date=7 November 2020|via=[[Newstalk ZB]] |date=18 October 2020}}</ref> When final results were announced on 6 November, this rose to 42 new members, the two additional new members being [[Emily Henderson (politician)|Emily Henderson]] (Labour) and [[Debbie Ngarewa-Packer]] (Māori).<ref><!-- this reference confirms that it's now 42 new members -->{{cite news |last1=Lynch |first1=Jenna |title=NZ Election 2020: Judith Collins will 'definitely not' stand down as leader despite National's crushing defeat |url= https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/11/nz-election-2020-judith-collins-will-definitely-not-stand-down-as-leader-despite-national-s-crushing-defeat.html |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20201106055203/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/11/nz-election-2020-judith-collins-will-definitely-not-stand-down-as-leader-despite-national-s-crushing-defeat.html |url-status= dead |archive-date= 6 November 2020 |accessdate=7 November 2020 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=6 November 2020}}</ref><ref><!-- this source names the two new members -->{{cite news |last1=Moir |first1=Jo |title=Special votes: National loses two MPs, one each to Labour, Māori Party |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/election-2020/430006/special-votes-national-loses-two-mps-one-each-to-labour-maori-party |accessdate=7 November 2020 |work=[[Radio New Zealand]] |date=6 November 2020}}</ref>

